examples.question_text:
A rowing team's mean mass is $72$ kg. Describe how the mean changes if:
(a) a rower of mass $84$ kg joins;
(b) a rower of mass $72$ kg joins;
(c) a rower of mass $60$ kg joins;
(d) the lightest rower, whose mass is below $72$ kg, leaves.

The graphs show a volunteer's hours before and after a fifth week is included. State whether the mean, median and range increase, decrease or stay the same. Show your working.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.55cm,y=0.22cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\path[use as bounding box] (-1.8,-7) rectangle (15,15);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,12);
\foreach \y in {0,2,4,6,8,10}{\draw (-0.12,\y)--(0,\y);\path (-0.18,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\foreach \x/\h in {1/4,2/6,3/8,4/10}{\draw (\x-0.3,0) rectangle (\x+0.3,\h);\path (\x,-0.5) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\path (2.5,-4.5) node[anchor=north] {Week};
\path (-1.3,6) node[rotate=90] {Hours};
\path (2.5,14) node {Before};
\begin{scope}[xshift=4.8cm]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,12);
\foreach \y in {0,2,4,6,8,10}{\draw (-0.12,\y)--(0,\y);\path (-0.18,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\foreach \x/\h in {1/4,2/6,3/8,4/10,5/2}{\draw (\x-0.3,0) rectangle (\x+0.3,\h);\path (\x,-0.5) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};}
\path (3,-4.5) node[anchor=north] {Week};
\path (-1.3,6) node[rotate=90] {Hours};
\path (3,14) node {After};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
